<p>President Trump said Monday that the U.S.-Iran ceasefire was on “massive life support” after rejecting Tehran’s latest counterproposal to end the war, calling it “totally unacceptable” and “a piece of garbage”. The ceasefire, in force since April 7 according to The Guardian, has largely halted fighting in the Gulf for more than a month, but talks remain deadlocked over nuclear concessions, the Strait of Hormuz and Iranian demands for the release of frozen assets and an end to the U.S. blockade. Iranian officials defended their counterproposal, while parliamentary speaker Mohammad Bagher Ghalibaf said Iran was prepared “for any eventuality” and ready to respond to aggression. Trump said he was considering reviving U.S. naval escorts through the Strait of Hormuz, and PBS reported that the administration announced new sanctions and that Trump planned to meet top military commanders to discuss next steps. The standoff has disrupted energy markets and commercial shipping through the Strait of Hormuz, with oil prices rising after Trump’s rejection. CBS News reported that Trump is expected to press China to pressure Iran during a Beijing visit this week, while Dawn reported that regional and international actors were trying to prevent a return to open hostilities.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/zrWxDP4EowzTX749t9s1M4D06i0XURPgW97VyLXdbcNnJw7qmcxV2jjuzP7laVCf3kjPbwd1TW7e8ugVfURTtFZ52oRfznCOul_EE9YmiX8b7kagqY9iDK2Z7t4V70XZhcXR8p63Brt8MwLJPwdojrqmqZXx6koK5VKKETk6HCixr-slS78rpwJ7f5b0CknzbhZmNzouTX7eq9D-E2AtM8yCoZ9gfvN3Y_JW9MH1fkh3BOsUAvamxggPuA' alt='President Donald Trump speaks at a dinner in the White House Rose Garden, on May 11, 2026, in Washington.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Negotiating gap: Trump said Iranian negotiators had verbally indicated willingness to let the United States remove Iran’s enriched-uranium stockpile, but later omitted that commitment from official documents.</li><li>Military posture: Axios, cited by RT, reported that U.S. options under discussion included renewed airstrikes and strikes on remaining Pentagon-identified targets, while Semafor said the U.S. Navy advertised a nuclear-armed submarine near the Mediterranean.</li><li>Regional spillover: AP reported exchanges of fire in recent days, attacks on ships and Gulf states, and renewed fighting between Israel and Hezbollah in Lebanon.</li></ul><blockquote>The energy supply shock that began in the first quarter is the largest the world has ever experienced. - Amin Nasser</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>White House: President Trump said the United States would seek “complete victory” over Iran and argued Tehran’s leadership expected him to lose interest in the conflict. (<a href='https://www.politico.com/news/2026/05/11/trump-iran-ceasefire-life-support-00914197'>Politico</a>)</li><li>Mohammad Bagher Ghalibaf: Iran’s parliamentary speaker said the United States had “no alternative” but to accept Tehran’s terms and warned that delay would raise costs for U.S. taxpayers. (<a href='https://www.rferl.org/a/iran-war-us-hormuz-oil-blockade-gulf-israel/33640284.html'>Radio Free Europe/Radio Liberty</a>)</li><li>Dawn: The Pakistani outlet reported that Washington appeared to believe sustained military and economic pressure could force major concessions, while Iranian officials believed they had already weathered the most dangerous phase. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1999572/pakistan-pushes-diplomatic-track-as-us-iran-hit-stall-mate'>Dawn</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://japantoday.com/category/world/trump-says-iran-ceasefire-is-%27on-life-support%27-as-hopes-for-a-deal-fade'>Trump says Iran ceasefire is &#x27;on life support&#x27; as hopes for a deal fade</a> - japantoday.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ft.com/content/69e836e6-b676-434f-9383-4522dc0c4eca'>Trump says Iran ceasefire is on ‘life support’</a> - ft.com</li><li><a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/international/article/2026/05/12/trump-warns-middle-